Ported files
------------
Bas Nijholt authored the files listed in docs/provenance/portable.tsv (first
import) and docs/provenance/portable-wave2.tsv (second import), both copied
from MindRoom Chat (mindroom-ai/mindroom-chat) at commit fc3a5905. Per his
instruction of 2026-11-02, he licenses the lines he wrote in the files of both
imports under the Apache License, Version 2.0 for this project. Lines by any
other author were blanked when copied (docs/provenance/holes.tsv and
holes-wave2.tsv) and written fresh here. docs/provenance/import.txt names the
import commits; docs/provenance.md describes the process.

Third-party notices
-------------------
mindroom-client installs its dependencies from npm under their own licenses;
package-lock.json pins the exact versions, and the notices each package ships
stay with that package. scripts/license-check.mjs accepts these licenses:
MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, 0BSD, Zlib,
Unicode-DFS-2016, Unicode-3.0, CC0-1.0, BlueOak-1.0.0, OFL-1.1 (fonts),
MPL-2.0 (used unmodified), Python-2.0 (argparse), and Unlicense (big-integer
and stream-buffers, under @capacitor/cli). It accepts three packages by name:
require-like (MIT license text, no license field), caniuse-lite (CC-BY-4.0
browser data, build tooling only, not in the bundle), and jsonify (public
domain, development only).

